<title>JAPAN: Hisamitsu to issue warrants as employee incentive.</title>
<headline>Hisamitsu to issue warrants as employee incentive.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hisamitsu Pharmaceutical Co Inc said on Monday that it would issue warrant bonds worth 1.25 billion yen to introduce an employee incentive plan.</p>
<p>Details of the bonds are as follows:</p>
<p>LEAD MGR - Nikko Securities Co Ltd</p>
<p>ISSUE NO 1		  AMT 1.25 bln yen</p>
<p>ISS PRICE 100 yen	 MATURITY 25.June, 2001</p>
<p>EXCERCISE FRM 1.Aug.97  EXERCISE TO 22.Jun.2001</p>
<p>PAY DATE 25.June.97     INT PAY 25.June-December.</p>
<p>SUB DATE 13-24.June.97</p>
<p>NOTE: The coupon and exercise price will be decided on June 11.</p>
</text>
